al fixed release on the current 2.x line.\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `6c69ace862`: passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-cve-2026-31337-fastjson-2.9.4", "confidence": 0.9}, "confidence": 0.9}, {"t_ms": 373581, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_015dx8v6tC3HcQWYM1Qs67Px", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-cve-2026-31337-fastjson-2.9.4", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 373581, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_015dx8v6tC3HcQWYM1Qs67Px", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 375459, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I upgraded fastjson from 2.8.0 to 2.9.4, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Advisory:** CVE-2026-31337 is a high-severity unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays. It affects fastjson below 2.9.4 and 3.0.0 up to 3.1.0. I chose 2.9.4 because it is the smallest fixed release on the current 2.x line.\n- **Branch:** `fix/cve-2026-31337-fastjson-2.9.4`, with two changes: the pin in `requirements.txt` and a line under \"Unreleased\" in `CHANGELOG.md`.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` on commit `6c69ace862` passed.\n- **PR:** #101, https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101.\n\nThe PR is open, not merged. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner under org policy.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by checking the advisory and finding where fastjson is pinned.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01S89SwKc8jW5dSyayCrM6Yw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "CVE-2026-31337", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, 